 can no longer be used. See Get Updates for the btp CLI.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2673 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Error Message for Non-Assigned Roles\nDescription: We've reworked the information screen that is shown if no roles are assigned for a user.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2674 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.7.0\nDescription:   This release contains Istio in version 1.21.3. For more details, read Istio 1.21.3 Release Announcement and Change Notes. See the changelog.  Now, you can opt out of the <ENABLE_EXTERNAL_NAME_ALIAS> Istio pilot environment variable in the Istio custom resource. This allows for retaining behavior that was present in Istio prior to version 1.21. See Istio Custom Resource Annotations.  We've added Request Authentication UI for Kyma dashboard.  Istio Operator does not restart Pods with the Istio sidecar that contain custom image annotations. See Resource Annotations.  We've changed Istio Ingress Gateway's scaling to be based only on CPU utilization. This adjustment ensures that the scaling is more responsive to traffic changes, as the Istio Ingress Gateway memory utilization is not a good indicator of the traffic load.  The default number of Istio Ingress Gateway replicas in smaller clusters is now set to 1.  We've introduced the compatibility mode, which allows you to mitigate breaking changes when a new Istio module's release introduces an Istio upgrade. The Istio module supports compatibility with the previous minor version of Istio. See Compatibility Mode.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2675 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Improved ML Models for Invoice, Purchase Order, and Payment Advice.\nDescription: We’ve improved the machine learning models for the document types invoice, purchase order, and payment advice.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2676 ---\nComponent: Platform Domains\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: TLS 1.3 Support\nDescription: TLS 1.3, the latest version of the security protocol, brings significant improvements over TLS 1.2 by offering enhanced security, better performance, and increased privacy. Consequently, TLS 1.3 is planned to be enabled for all platform domains in the Neo environment by the end of June 2024. Furthermore, TLS 1.2 remains as a fallback option.  The following domains are adjusted:      *.<Region.Domain>      *.dispatcher.<Region.Domain>      *.cert.<Region.Domain>      *.static.<Region.Domain>      connectivitynotification.<Region.Domain>      connectivitytunnel.<Region.Domain>      For more information, see SAP Note 3435199 .  Action: During the transition period, until TLS 1.3 is fully enabled by the end of June 2024, we recommend you verify your clients by connecting them to the following URL (applicable for TLS 1.3 and TLS 1.2): https://account.ca1.hana.ondemand.com/#/home/welcome.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-02\nValid as Of: 2024-06-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2677 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   General availability of SAP Translation Hub in the BTP multi-environment   \nDescription:   SAP Translation Hub is now generally available in the BTP multi-environment (e.g. 